[95.167308, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped every date to the 28th, then advanced from the\n  previous renewal. Renewals now clamp to the target month's actual last day\n  and always derive from the original anchor, restoring month-end and leap-day\n  anniversaries. Cycle lookup also avoids scanning all previous renewals.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and the old price on the change date.\n  It now uses actual cycle days and the old price in force at cycle start.\n- Same-interval changes retain their anchor; interval changes charge the full\n  new price and re-anchor on the change date. Invoice lines cover their\n  respective credited and charged periods.\n- Half-even rounding now uses exact integer arithmetic, independent of Decimal\n  precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n- Added calendar, rounding, interval-change, invoice, and real CLI regression\n  tests, including CLI verification of all finance worked examples.\n\n## Release blocker: missing"]
[95.167358, "i", " approved partner data\n\nThe full suite had a separate error before these changes and still fails at\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` for `sub_1151`:\n`KeyError: 'P-31'`. `data/subscriptions.json` references partner P-31, but\n`data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17 and P-24. No P-31 commission rate\nor contract is supplied in the repository.\n\nFinance must supply the approved P-31 partner record/rate (or an authoritative\ncorrection to the subscription's partner assignment). No rate was guessed,\nno partner data was removed, and no tests were skipped or quarantined.\nThe release is NOT ready while this error remains. After correcting the data,\nrerun:\n\n    cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\nEOF\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[95.170649, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
